    <section aria-labelledby="article-components">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2 id="article-components">Shared content styling</h2>
        <p>Posts, notes, and pages share these headings, quotes, callouts, and interactive details.</p>
        <blockquote>
          <p>A good personal site should feel calm, readable, and unmistakably yours.</p>
        </blockquote>

        {% articleCallout "In practice" %}
Keep the useful instruction beside the explanation. A short callout gives it room without interrupting the rest of the article.
        {% endarticleCallout %}

        {% articleCallout "Example", "example" %}
A vendor advisory and a software inventory may use different names for the same product. A precise version range helps connect the two.
        {% endarticleCallout %}

        {% articleCallout "A limitation", "caution" %}
A matching version is a reason to investigate. It does not, by itself, establish whether a vulnerable feature is reachable in a particular environment.
        {% endarticleCallout %}

        <h3>Supporting detail, when you want it</h3>
        {% articleDetails "See the product-matching example" %}
An advisory might cover one release branch while another already contains the fix. Compare the installed version with the vendor's affected range before deciding which systems need attention.

The main explanation stays visible in the article; this panel holds the additional example.
        {% endarticleDetails %}

        {% articleSteps "From an advisory to a response", [
          {title: "Read the advisory", text: "Identify the product and affected versions."},
          {title: "Check the inventory", text: "Find candidate systems and investigate exposure."},
          {title: "Verify the result", text: "Confirm the mitigation or update took effect."}
        ] %}

        {% articleDetails "Show the article formatting examples" %}
Use a callout for a short practical point:

```njk
{% raw %}{% articleCallout "In practice" %}
Your paragraph, with **Markdown** if needed.
{% endarticleCallout %}{% endraw %}
```

Use an expandable panel for optional background:

```njk
{% raw %}{% articleDetails "See the example" %}
The supporting explanation goes here.
{% endarticleDetails %}{% endraw %}
```

The contents section appears automatically on articles with at least three main headings. Set `toc: false` in an article's front matter to omit it.
        {% endarticleDetails %}
